§5 ⚜ ᴀ ꜱᴛᴏʀʏ ꜱᴇʀɪᴇꜱ ⚜
#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2  ʜᴇʀᴇ ʙᴇ ᴅʀᴀɢᴏɴꜱ...
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2Fern and Castien arrived safely back at The Spyglass Tavern where they had initially met. After a LOT of drinks and realising they left Honey The Bee behind all this time, they set their sights on the real End.§r
#- §2They couldn’t stop thinking about the portal that §5ɨȶ §2had led them to. Fern thought it was all a trick, an illusion. But Castien believed something went wrong and that’s why Sweetpea saved them. He believed The End was still there, and he joked that this was a huge ‘Loose End’. Fern laughed.
#- §2Castien began telling Fern all kinds of stories that foretold the merging of the mortal realm and The End dimension, bringing chaos and destruction upon all. To prevent this cataclysm, someone needed to embark on a treacherous quest to defeat the mighty Ender Dragon;§r
#- §2The Guardian of The End. Fern made it very clear that whenever Castien said ‘someone’ he always meant ‘her’ and that he should stop doing that. The elf prince smiled and plonked The Emerald Crown on her head. She blushed. 

Many more drinks later it was decided!§r
#- §2With determination, Fern and Castien set forth back to the portal. Their bond strengthens with every step. Finally, after weeks of arduous travel, they reached the ominous gateway to The End. A swirling vortex of blue and black stars loomed before them, an eerie hum...§r
#- §2As they jumped a leap of faith through the portal, the air turned heavy and the sky darkened. The End was a desolate expanse, with floating islands suspended above an abyss. The ground trembled beneath their feet as the ominous roar of the Ender Dragon echoed through the§r
#- §2void. With Castien's ancient arcane knowledge guiding them, they devised a plan. Fern, wielding her trusty sword, would engage the fearsome beast in combat, while Castien used his elven magic to distract, attack and shield her from harm. 

The battle raged on...§r
#- §2The Ender Dragon unleashing its wrath upon them. Fern dodged its devastating attacks with lightning reflexes, her sword glinting with determination. Castien's enchantments deflected the dragon's onslaught, buying Fern precious moments to strike.§r
#- §2With every swing of her blade, Fern chipped away at the dragon's defences, her strikes fueled by the unwavering belief that she could protect her world. As the battle neared its climax, the dragon weakened, its roars growing feeble. Summoning every ounce of her energy,§r
#- §2Fern delivered a final, mighty blow with her sword. The blade pierced through the dragon's heart, releasing a blinding explosion of light. 
The majestic creature let out a final, mournful cry before dissolving into particles, leaving behind a shower of purple crystals.§r
#- §2As the dust settled, Fern and Castien stood victorious, their faces adorned with a mixture of exhaustion and triumph. The End dimension quivered as if recognizing the heroism that had saved it from destruction. The gateway began to close, and Fern and Castien hurriedly§r
#- §2made their way back to the mortal realm. 

Returning to Craftadia, they were hailed as heroes, their names whispered in awe by grateful villagers. Fern, forever changed by her journey, shared tales of her bravery, reminding all that even in the face of§r
#- §2darkness, hope and courage could prevail.

§c"The End. That is it for today kids! Time for sleep now, goodnight." §8said Uncle Yoshi. §c"Goodnight" §8said three bright eyed dragons, named Snow, Sparky and Ember, all at the same time. They one by one slowly drifted into slumber...
